17F96: 'sub_17F96' -> 'findMonsterAtPosition'
    Called from canMoveToTile (with dl/dh=the candidate X/Y). Loops updateMonsterAI's 32-slot overworld monster arrays (base `+0x1280`=type/`+0x12C0`=X/`+0x12E0`=Y, same convention confirmed elsewhere), skipping empty slots (`type==0`), looking for one whose X/Y matches. Returns bx=0FFFFh if no monster occupies that position. This is the overworld's 32-slot counterpart to findCombatantAtPosition's 8-slot combat-arena lookup -- same purpose (don't let two monsters/movers occupy the same tile), different array.
128F2: 'sub_128F2' -> 'getDungeonTileAt'
    NOT actually one of canMoveToTile's helpers (an earlier roadmap note guessed it was, alongside findMonsterAtPosition -- canMoveToTile in fact only calls findMonsterAtPosition; this correction supersedes that note). Computes a dungeon map byte offset from packed (X,Y) in (bl,bh) -- `bh<<4 | bl` -- plus `_dungeonLevel<<8`, added to a fixed base (`0x900`), and reads the tile byte there. This is the dungeon-map counterpart to getMapTileAt (overworld/town), reading directly from a loaded per-level dungeon buffer rather than computing a packed-tile value.

